<title>GERMANY: George-no advantage for UK to rejoin current ERM.</title>
<headline>George-no advantage for UK to rejoin current ERM.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of England Governor Eddie George said on Tuesday it would be of no advantage to Britain if it rejoined the current Exchange Rate Mechanism.</p>
<p>George also said during a panel discussion at the Global 24 conference here that he saw no question that core European currencies were being affected by European monetary union.</p>
<p>George also said that markets were &quot;assuming there will be a fairly broadly based euro.&quot;</p>
<p>The bond market, and to a degree the foreign exchange markets, were trading on that basis, George said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
